                    <msContents>
                        <summary/>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i1">               
                            <locus from="1" to="20"/>
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1467GadlaI">Gadla ʾIyasus Moʾa</title>
                            <note>According to a note by <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3182ContiRo">Carlo Conti Rossini</persName> (cf. <ref target="#a1"/>), the text was copied 
                                from a manuscript of ‘Ḥayq’, which refers probably to the monastery <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0327DHE">Dabra Ḥayq ʾƎsṭifānos</placeName>.
                                The manuscript was used by Stanislas Kur in his edition <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/XPPMH5CB"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Kur1965IyasusMoa"/><title level="m">Actes de Iyasus Moʿa, abbé du Convent de St-Etienne de Ḥayq, Textus, Versio</title><title level="s">Corpus Scriptorum Christianorum Orientalium</title><author><forename>Stanislas</forename><surname>Kur</surname></author><editor><forename>Stanislas</forename><surname>Kur</surname></editor><pubPlace>Louvain</pubPlace><publisher>Secrétariat Du CorpusSCO</publisher><date>1965</date><series><title level="s">Corpus Scriptorum Christianorum Orientalium</title><biblScope unit="volume">259, 260, Scriptores Aethiopici, 49, 50</biblScope></series><biblScope unit="volume">259, 260, Scriptores Aethiopici, 49, 50</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Kur1965IyasusMoa</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Kur1965IyasusMoa</note></bibl>
                                with the siglum ‘B’. Some parts of the text have been published and translated by Carlo Conti Rossini, as well:
                                <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/AXPDULBX"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:ContiRossini1922Zague"/><title level="a">La caduta della dinastia Zagué e la versione amarica del Beʿela Nagast</title><title level="j">Rendiconti della Reale Accademia dei Lincei, Classe di scienze morali, storiche e filologiche</title><author><forename>Carlo</forename><surname>Conti Rossini</surname></author><date>1922</date><biblScope unit="volume">Serie quinta, vol. 31</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">228–291</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:ContiRossini1922Zague</note></note><note type="tag">bm:ContiRossini1922Zague</note></bibl>. An unpublished Italian translation is attested in 
                                manuscript Conti Rossini 121 in the same collection in the Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei. 
                                The manuscript consists of two quires, which are not in the correct order. The text starts on <locus target="#11r"/>.
                                The second half of the text is placed in front on <locus from="1" to="10"/>.
                                It is wrongly attributed ‘KRZ 82’ in <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/N6HPGQK3"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue"/><title level="m">Catalogue des manuscrits éthiopiens de l’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei: Fonds Conti Rossini et Fonds Caetani 209, 375, 376, 377, 378</title><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><author><forename>Stefan</forename><surname>Strelcyn</surname></author><pubPlace>Roma</pubPlace><publisher>Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei</publisher><date>1976</date><series><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope></series><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note></note><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note><citedRange unit="page">221</citedRange></bibl>, which is in fact  ‘KRZ 86’ (= Kinefe-Rigb Zelleke 86).</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
